## How the acceptance criteria are met

| # | Criterion | Where |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Bucket versioned, encrypted, non-public | `aws_s3_bucket_versioning`, `..._server_side_encryption_configuration` (AES256 dev / KMS prod), `..._public_access_block` all-true, `BucketOwnerEnforced`, TLS-only bucket policy |
| 2 | RDS hardened | `deletion_protection = true`, `backup_retention_period` validated `>= 7` (30 in prod), `publicly_accessible = false`, `storage_encrypted = true`, private subnet group, SG ingress only from named client SGs |
| 3 | Secret never plaintext in Git | Generated by `random_password`, written to Secrets Manager (CMK-encrypted in prod). Root module exports the **ARN only**. State lives in an encrypted, DynamoDB-locked S3 backend |
| 4 | Least privilege, no prod wildcards | Policy scoped to one bucket ARN, one secret ARN, two KMS actions. A `precondition` on `terraform_data.no_wildcards_in_prod` fails the plan if any `*` or `service:*` action/resource appears when `environment == "prod"` |
| 7 | Environment isolation | Distinct backend `key` per env; no shared workspace state. Providers, sizing, encryption posture, and trust model all differ by tfvars |

**Out of scope for this module** (per the task's three-resource brief): EKS node groups (criterion 5) and CloudFront/ACM (criterion 6). They belong in sibling modules — `modules/eks/` consumes `service_account.role_arn` for IRSA and exports its node SG into `db_client_security_group_ids`; `modules/cdn/` consumes `assets.bucket_domain_name` via OAC. The wiring points are already exposed as outputs above.
